{
  "dom_id": "step-e13396",
  "name": "Example: Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number Resulting in a Mixed Number",
  "problem": "Find the value $9\\times\\dfrac 3 {4}$ as a mixed number.",
  "worked_solution": "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n9\\times \\dfrac{3}{4} = \\dfrac{9\\times 3}{4} = \\dfrac{27}{4}\n$$\n\nWe now convert this to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n27\\div 4 = 6\\,\\textrm{R} 3 = 6\\,\\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$",
